## Two String-typed parameters compared via `==`. Before the fix in
## task #22, both `s` and `needle` were typed `Ty::Class { name:
## "String" }` (the resolve-pass anchored the user-side `class String`
## onto the same DefId as the primitive `Ty::String` TypeAlias and then
## stomped the kind to `DefKind::Class`). The codegen
## `is_string_mir_ty` helper only recognised the canonical `Ty::String`
## / `Ty::Str` forms, so the `Compare` emitter fell back to integer
## pointer-eq for `s == needle`. Two byte-identical heap Strings then
## compared unequal silently.

def check_strings(s: String, needle: String) -> Int
  if s == needle
    1
  else
    0
  end
end

def main
  let a = String.from("hello")
  let b = String.from("hello")
  let r = check_strings(a, b)
  if r == 1
    puts "match"
  else
    puts "fail"
  end
end
